# Keep these out of the Docker build context entirely. Two reasons:
#   1) Smaller image, faster builds.
#   2) Defence-in-depth — nothing in `.env`/`server/.env` can ever ride
#      into a `COPY` directive by accident and then override Fly secrets
#      at runtime via dotenv. Trainer-app got bitten by exactly this: a
#      stale local key overrode a rotated Fly secret because server/.env
#      had been silently baked into the image.
node_modules
dist
.git
.github
.vercel
.fly
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
